    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for gfs2-utils.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 8.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "The gfs2-utils packages contain utilities for creating, checking, modifying, and correcting any inconsistencies in GFS2 global file systems.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* gfs2-utils: gfs2-utils: stack out-of-bounds write via unchecked height in savemeta (CVE-2026-71221)\n\n* gfs2-utils: gfs2-utils: stack out-of-bounds write via unchecked di_height in gfs2_edit (CVE-2026-71220)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
        "text": "This content is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). If you distribute this content, or a modified version of it, you must provide attribution to the original copyright holder(s) and provide a link to the original.",
